<!--
  The MERGED Backup screen (toolbar title "Backup") — the encrypted downloads
  backup into a folder of the user's choosing IS the screen; bookmarks and key
  plumbing are secondary. The folder is whatever the system picker offers —
  Google Drive, Dropbox, Nextcloud, an SD card, the phone itself — and no
  Firedown server is involved (the hosted service this replaced is gone).
  Layout, in priority order:

    ── (flat, on the page) ──
       CloudStatusPreference   the status card: "Back up your downloads" +
                               [Set up backup] (creates the recovery code,
                               then "Where to back up"), the backed-up size
                               once set up, or the lost folder + [Choose the
                               folder again] / [Reconnect]
    ── three UNLABELLED card groups (title-less PreferenceCategory) ──
       KEY group   Recovery code (shown once a key exists; the reveal dialog
                   carries Copy AND Save-to-file) · I have a recovery code
                   (adopt / replace the key)
       USE group   Backup folder (where it is; tap = change) · Backups
                   (set-up gated) · Sync bookmarks (INLINE switch,
                   secondary by design; "Sync now" dropped — sync is
                   automatic, the summary shows last-synced)
       last        How sync & encryption work · Delete backup data (the ONE
                   erasure door, LAST by danger)
    The KEY and USE groups swap by LIFE STAGE (SyncSettingsFragment
    .updateState): KEY above USE until the backup is set up — the second way
    in sits right under the setup card while there is nothing else to reach —
    then USE above KEY, the daily-use rows first. Swapping GROUPS, not rows,
    keeps each group whole in both stages.

  The groups carry NO labels on purpose. Headers were dissolved from this
  screen one by one ("Manage backup" / "Recovery code" / "About" over one row
  each restated the row, and the last "Bookmarks" header umbrella'd the
  code/FAQ/delete rows under it — "why is Delete backed-up files under
  Bookmarks?"). A title-less category draws no text: the CARD edges do the
  grouping, so the old "a header owns every row until the next one" trap
  cannot come back.

  KEY-FIRST GATE: a recovery code is the gateway. "Set up backup" creates it
  (with the "I've saved it" step) before it opens the place chooser, the
  Backups row is hidden and the Bookmarks switch is DISABLED until one
  exists — a folder can only be chosen once there is a key to encrypt into
  it with.

  The bookmarks-list overflow + sync banner deep-links (EXTRA_OPEN_BOOKMARKS_SYNC)
  land HERE. Backing up stays action-driven (a download's options sheet backs
  it up on demand). The debug account-id row (debug builds only) is appended
  programmatically by SyncSettingsFragment.
-->
<PreferenceScreen xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto">

    <!-- The status CARD (Signal's shape: where, how much, and at most one
         button inside it — "Set up backup" or the lost folder's remedy),
         bound by SyncSettingsFragment. Custom layout — no title/icon. -->
    <com.solarized.firedown.settings.CloudStatusPreference
        android:key="com.solarized.firedown.preferences.cloud.backup.status"
        android:selectable="false"
        android:persistent="false" />

    <!-- KEY group (title-less: a card group, no label). XML position (above
         the USE group) is the ONBOARDING order; updateState() swaps the two
         groups once the backup is set up. -->
    <PreferenceCategory
        android:key="com.solarized.firedown.preferences.cloud.group.key"
        android:persistent="false">

        <!-- ONE recovery-code row (was Show + Save-to-file, two rows and two
             device-auth prompts for the same object): the reveal dialog behind the
             single auth now carries Copy AND Save-to-file — export is something
             you do while LOOKING at the code, so the reveal is where you reach for
             it. Title reuses the old category header string ("Recovery code").
             Shown once a key exists, so pre-key the adopt door below is the
             group's only row. -->
        <Preference
            android:key="com.solarized.firedown.preferences.sync.show.code"
            android:title="@string/settings_sync_cat_code"
            android:summary="@string/settings_sync_show_code_shared_summary"
            app:singleLineTitle="false"
            app:icon="@drawable/ic_key_24" />

        <!-- The adopt-an-existing-key door (the setup card above covers Create;
             post-key this row is a REPLACE — see SyncSettingsFragment). It shares
             a card group with the Recovery code row: the two are the key's two
             doors (see yours / use another one). Shield-with-keyhole glyph
             (encrypted_24), not the key: the key glyph belongs to the Recovery
             code reveal row, and two different rows wearing the same object read
             as duplicates. (It wore ic_login_24 first — an arrow into a ring,
             which read as "sign in" on a screen that has no accounts.) -->
        <Preference
            android:key="com.solarized.firedown.preferences.sync.link.code"
            android:title="@string/settings_sync_link_title"
            android:summary="@string/settings_sync_link_summary"
            app:singleLineTitle="false"
            app:icon="@drawable/encrypted_24" />

    </PreferenceCategory>

    <!-- USE group (title-less): the daily-use rows. Above the KEY group once
         the backup is set up (updateState). -->
    <PreferenceCategory
        android:key="com.solarized.firedown.preferences.cloud.group.use"
        android:persistent="false">

        <!-- WHERE the backup is — "Google Drive › Backups" as the summary — and
             the ONE door to change it (SyncSettingsFragment.changeFolder:
             confirmed while the folder holds files, since the old folder keeps
             them and they leave the Backups list until it is chosen again). A
             ROW, not a button: "Change folder" was the most prominent control
             on a healthy backup, a verb with no object, and the question it
             provoked — change it to what, from what? — is answered by stating
             the folder, the way Signal, Aegis and Syncthing state their backup
             path on a row. Visible once a folder is chosen. -->
        <Preference
            android:key="com.solarized.firedown.preferences.cloud.backup.folder"
            android:title="@string/folder_backup_row_title"
            app:singleLineTitle="false"
            app:icon="@drawable/folder_24" />

        <!-- Visible once the backup is set up (a key AND a folder). No "Manage
             backup" label: over this row it restated the row (the same
             taxonomy-noise argument that dissolved the Cookies category), and the
             row already sits in backup context under the status card. -->
        <Preference
            android:key="com.solarized.firedown.preferences.cloud.backup.files"
            android:title="@string/cloud_backup_files_title"
            android:summary="@string/settings_cloud_backup_files_summary"
            app:singleLineTitle="false"
            app:icon="@drawable/cloud_upload_24" />

        <!-- Bookmarks are deliberately SECONDARY on this screen: ONE inline switch
             (sync is automatic once on — change-triggered + on-toggle — so the old
             focused screen's "Sync now" row was reassurance theater and is gone;
             the last-synced summary carries the same signal). The switch never
             self-persists: SyncManager owns SYNC_ENABLED, the fragment re-syncs
             checked state from isEnabled(). NO "Bookmarks" label — it was the LAST
             header on the screen (kept as a separator), but a labelled header
             visually owns every row until the NEXT one, so with the other headers
             dissolved it umbrella'd the recovery-code/FAQ/delete rows as
             "Bookmarks" children ("why is Delete backed-up files under
             Bookmarks?"). The card group's edge now ends where its rows end. -->
        <SwitchPreferenceCompat
            android:key="com.solarized.firedown.preferences.sync.enabled"
            android:title="@string/settings_sync_title"
            android:summary="@string/settings_sync_switch_summary"
            app:singleLineTitle="false"
            app:icon="@drawable/ic_bookmarks_24" />

    </PreferenceCategory>

    <!-- Last group (title-less): what the backup is, and how to leave it. -->
    <PreferenceCategory
        android:key="com.solarized.firedown.preferences.cloud.group.about"
        android:persistent="false">

        <!-- A LINK to the website's /security page (opened in a Firedown tab via
             the OPEN_URI result handshake, like the Donate row). It replaced an
             offline nine-question FAQ sub-screen: seven of the nine were
             reassurance copy the website owns, and the two load-bearing facts
             (the code is the only key — no reset; Safe Folder never leaves the
             device) are already stated in-app at their points of action, the
             reveal dialog and the multi-select backup snackbar. Summary = the
             URL, so the row says it leaves the app. -->
        <Preference
            android:key="com.solarized.firedown.preferences.sync.help"
            android:title="@string/settings_sync_help_title"
            android:summary="@string/settings_sync_help_url_display"
            app:singleLineTitle="false"
            app:icon="@drawable/encryption_24" />

        <!-- The destructive actions sit LAST — placement by danger, not taxonomy —
             behind ONE door → the "Delete backup data" SUB-SCREEN
             (settings_cloud_delete.xml / CloudDeleteFragment), two rows of the
             SCOPED erasures (never one "delete everything", which would couple
             wiping free bookmarks to destroying the backed-up files):
             bookmarks-from-server while sync is on, backed-up-files under the
             Backups row's set-up gate. A screen, not a chooser dialog (which
             shipped for a commit): its rows carry each deletion's consequence as
             the summary, so the choice is informed before the confirm. Deleting
             the files does NOT forget the folder or the key. Hidden when neither
             applies. -->
        <Preference
            android:key="com.solarized.firedown.preferences.cloud.delete"
            android:title="@string/settings_cloud_delete_title"
            android:summary="@string/settings_cloud_delete_summary"
            app:singleLineTitle="false"
            app:icon="@drawable/ic_baseline_delete_24" />

    </PreferenceCategory>

</PreferenceScreen>
